    {
      "start": 0.119,
      "end": 0.299,
      "text": "So"
    },
    {
      "start": 0.799,
      "end": 1.559,
      "text": "welcome back again."
    },
    {
      "start": 1.979,
      "end": 3.179,
      "text": "Time for one more problem."
    },
    {
      "start": 3.619,
      "end": 4.319,
      "text": "Now, in this problem,"
    },
    {
      "start": 4.779,
      "end": 8.34,
      "text": "we are given that the speeds of two trains are in the ratio of seven is to nine."
    },
    {
      "start": 8.88,
      "end": 11.8,
      "text": "Also, the faster train covers one hundred eighty kilometer"
    },
    {
      "start": 12.239,
      "end": 13.059,
      "text": "in two hours."
    },
    {
      "start": 13.5,
      "end": 14.939,
      "text": "The question is asking us to find"
    },
    {
      "start": 15.399,
      "end": 16.799,
      "text": "the speed of the slower train."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.159,
      "end": 19.099,
      "text": "Because the ratio is seven is to nine,"
    },
    {
      "start": 19.539,
      "end": 26.679,
      "text": "let the speed of the slower train be seven x kilometer per hour, and let the speed of the faster train be nine x kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.139,
      "end": 28.299,
      "text": "Now, we know the formula,"
    },
    {
      "start": 28.799,
      "end": 31.319,
      "text": "speed is equal to distance divided by time."
    },
    {
      "start": 31.739,
      "end": 32.639,
      "text": "Putting the values,"
    },
    {
      "start": 33.099,
      "end": 36.559,
      "text": "speed of the faster train is equal to one hundred eighty divided by two."
    },
    {
      "start": 37.059,
      "end": 38.939,
      "text": "This gives us ninety kilometer per hour."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.5,
      "end": 49.119,
      "text": "Now that we know the actual speed of the faster train, we can equate it with the value we took earlier, which is nine x. So nine x is equal to ninety, x is equal to ten."
    },
    {
      "start": 49.479,
      "end": 53.779,
      "text": "Now, speed of the slower train is equal to seven into x, that is equal to seven into ten."
    },
    {
      "start": 54.259,
      "end": 61.299,
      "text": "So the speed of the slower train is seventy kilometer per hour. Hence, the correct answer is option A."
    }
  ],
